story: Petal & Stem at Dawn (fiction)
== the whole piece as one timed prompt
Photorealistic widescreen 16:9 ad with warm, natural light. A florist opens Petal & Stem at dawn, arranges a bouquet, and hands it to a smiling customer at the door. Same people, place and product throughout. The florist wears a cream shirt and sage apron. The customer wears a tan jacket. The shop is a small neighbourhood flower shop with a painted green door and wooden sign. The bouquet is one set of pink and cream flower stems, initially loose, then gathered and wrapped in kraft paper. 0–4 s: At dawn, a medium exterior tracks the florist approaching from outside, unlocking and opening the shop’s front door. Warm natural light catches the apron; the sign stays out of frame. 4–9 s: Cut inside to a close view of the florist’s hands gathering loose stems into one bouquet and wrapping it in kraft paper. A gentle push-in follows the work in warm natural window light. 9–13 s: Cut to a medium doorway two-shot: the florist hands that same wrapped bouquet to the smiling customer, who takes it securely. Warm dawn light falls across both faces; the sign remains outside the frame. 13–16 s: Cut to a steady, straight-on wide exterior of the neighbourhood shop front in warm natural dawn light. Hold the complete façade, with “Petal & Stem” clearly legible above the door. Wherever it is legible the lettering reads exactly "Petal & Stem", every letter right. No readable text except the final shop sign; no speech, voiceover, or music; no duplicate bouquet; always held or resting; silent: no speech, no voiceover.
